From: T3 Code (Hermes fork)
Subject: [PATCH] acp: honor the configured reasoning effort when building an agent

The ACP adapter is the only Hermes surface that does not route reasoning
effort through hermes_constants.resolve_reasoning_config. Every other
entry point (CLI startup, messaging gateway, Desktop/TUI, cron, /model
switch, fallback activation) resolves per-model
agent.reasoning_overrides over the global agent.reasoning_effort, but
_make_agent never passes reasoning_config to AIAgent, so agent_init
leaves it None and the provider default is used regardless of config.

config is already loaded in this function, so resolving there is enough.
Because set_session_model rebuilds the agent through _make_agent, a level
changed in config.yaml also takes effect on the next agent build rather
than only on process restart.

Verified against hermes-agent 3c108589fbcaa7284ac9b4b31c0f1c75ac76cd47.
---
--- a/acp_adapter/session.py
+++ b/acp_adapter/session.py
@@ -633,7 +633,22 @@
             "model": model or default_model,
         }

+        # Reasoning effort: route through the shared chokepoint every other
+        # surface uses (per-model ``agent.reasoning_overrides`` > global
+        # ``agent.reasoning_effort``). Without this the ACP surface is the
+        # only one that ignores the configured level and silently takes the
+        # provider default. Rebuilt agents (``set_session_model``) re-read it
+        # here, so a level change lands on the next agent build.
         try:
+            from hermes_constants import resolve_reasoning_config
+
+            kwargs["reasoning_config"] = resolve_reasoning_config(
+                config, kwargs["model"]
+            )
+        except Exception:
+            logger.debug("ACP: could not resolve reasoning config", exc_info=True)
+
+        try:
             runtime = resolve_runtime_provider(requested=requested_provider or config_provider)
             kwargs.update(
                 {
